      <guid>https://vishvAsa.github.io/AgamaH_brAhmaH/shAnkara-darshanam/tattvam/en/nitin-trasi/the-man-who-wasn-t-there/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;the-man-who-wasnt-there-dr-nitin-trasi&#34;&gt;The Man Who Wasn&amp;rsquo;t There Dr. Nitin Trasi&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Source: &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/discourses/teachers/manwho_trasi.htm&#34;&gt;TW&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Author: Dr. Nitin Trasi&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/8124601305/fromtheunreat-20&#34;&gt;&lt;figure class=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/images/science_nitin.JPG&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;img src=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/images/science_nitin.JPG&#34; alt=&#34;book cover&#34; title=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &#xA;&#xA;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Purchase Nitin Trasi&amp;rsquo;s book &amp;lsquo;&lt;a href=&#34;http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/8124601305/fromtheunreat-20&#34;&gt;The Science of Enlightenment&lt;/a&gt;&amp;rsquo;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Visit &lt;a href=&#34;http://www.geocities.com/nitin_trasi/&#34;&gt;Nitin &amp;rsquo;s website&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Link to entry in &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.advaita.org.uk/reading/read_general.htm#trasi&#34;&gt;Recommuended Books Section &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;THE MAN WHO WASN&amp;rsquo;T THERE&lt;br&gt;&#xA;(or &lt;em&gt;The Seeker&amp;rsquo;s Dilemma&lt;/em&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(with apologies to Ogden Nash)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Yesterday on the stair,&lt;br&gt;&#xA;I met a man who wasn&amp;rsquo;t there,&lt;br&gt;&#xA;He wasn&amp;rsquo;t there again today,&lt;br&gt;&#xA;I wish to God he&amp;rsquo;d go away.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I had come across this piece of nonsense verse earlier too, and saw it again a few days ago. It had never struck me before that this verse could have any spiritual significance, but this time it seemed to have a special meaning - it seemed to illustrate the typical dilemma of the spiritual seeker.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
